Subject: one job at a time per printer through an flock()ed file, not a boost named semaphore

The filter serialised its jobs on a boost::interprocess named_mutex (a POSIX
semaphore in /dev/shm) named after the CUPS destination it looked up from
argv[0]. When the lookup failed the name was empty and every job stopped
with "ERROR: Unable to get synchronization lock: Invalid argument"; a filter
killed while it held the semaphore (a cancelled job, a crash) left it taken,
so every later job waited 30 seconds and failed until the machine was
restarted; and a semaphore made by another user could not be opened by lp.

The lock is now an flock() on TMPDIR/dymo-lw-PRINTER.lock (CUPS's spool
tmp, which every filter shares as lp), PRINTER from the destination's
DymoLockName option, else its name, else $PRINTER: the kernel drops it with
its process. 30 seconds' wait as before. No more boost.
